### IPP-1704 Full access per language (all / some / none)
### Put ADMIN_PASSWORD from server/.env while testing, then put CHANGE_ME back.
### Needs 2+ active languages with topics (e.g. php + react). Change the slugs below if yours differ.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@adminEmail = askedin143@gmail.com
@adminPassword = Askedin-Admin-2026!x
@userEmail = arsalmustafa62+ipp2@gmail.com
@userPassword = Student-Test-123
@userSearch = arsalmustafa62%2Bipp2@gmail.com
@langA = react
@langB = php
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.data.token}}
@userToken = {{userLogin.response.body.data.token}}
@userId = {{userList.response.body.data.users.0._id}}
@langAId = {{langs.response.body.data.languages.0._id}}


### 1. Admin login -> 200
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }


### 2. Find the user -> 200, users[0] = that user ("+" sent as %2B, else the search finds nobody)
# @name userList
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/users?search={{userSearch}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 3. Language list (A-Z) -> 200. @langAId = FIRST language in this list; set @langA to its slug.
# @name langs
GET {{baseUrl}}/languages


### 4. Give ONLY language A -> 200 "... now has full access to <A>", user.accessScope = "some", paidLanguages = [A]
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/{{userId}}/access
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "access": "some", "languages": ["{{langAId}}"] }


### 5. 'some' with no languages -> 400 "Pick at least one language"
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/{{userId}}/access
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "access": "some", "languages": [] }


### 6. User login -> 200, user.paidLanguages = [{ _id, name, slug }]
# @name userLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{userEmail}}", "password": "{{userPassword}}" }


### 7. Languages as user -> A: hasAccess true, B: hasAccess false
GET {{baseUrl}}/languages
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### 8. Questions of A -> hasFullAccess true, hiddenCount 0, every topic, no isLocked
GET {{baseUrl}}/questions?language={{langA}}&limit=50
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### 9. Questions of B -> hasFullAccess false, only first topic, hiddenCount > 0
# @name langBQuestions
GET {{baseUrl}}/questions?language={{langB}}&limit=50
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 10. Quiz A -> 201, isSample false (6 MCQs)
POST {{baseUrl}}/quiz/start
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "language": "{{langA}}", "difficulty": "mixed" }


### 11. Quiz B -> 201, isSample true (sample quiz)
POST {{baseUrl}}/quiz/start
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "language": "{{langB}}" }


### 12. Bookmarks list -> 200 (allowed now: user has one language). Only language A questions.
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookmarks
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### 13. Bookmark a question of B (run step 9 first) -> 403 NEEDS_FULL_ACCESS
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookmarks/{{langBQuestions.response.body.data.questions.0._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### 14. All languages -> 200 "... full access to all languages", accessScope "all", paidLanguages []
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/{{userId}}/access
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "access": "all" }


### 15. No access -> 200 "Full access turned off", isPaid false. Then step 12 -> 403
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/{{userId}}/access
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "access": "none" }


### 16. Old body still works -> 200 (= all languages)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/{{userId}}/access
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isPaid": true }


### 17. Wrong access value -> 400 "access must be all, some or none"
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/{{userId}}/access
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "access": "gold" }


### Browser:
### - Admin -> Users -> Edit access -> "Only these languages" -> tick 1 -> Save -> badge shows the name
### - As that user: Languages page card of A shows all questions, B only the first topic; quiz B = sample
### - Dashboard plan badge = language names + "Add languages"; Pricing: "<A> unlocked", dropdown without A
### - Existing paid users still have every language (nothing to change)
